questions.answer:
- **Losses**, including deficiencies of capital, are paid first out of profits, next out of capital, and lastly, if necessary, by partners individually in their profit-sharing ratio.
- **Assets** of the firm, including sums contributed by partners to make up capital deficiencies, are applied in this order:
- (a) paying debts of the firm to third parties;
- (b) paying each partner rateably what is due to him for advances (loans) as distinguished from capital;
- (c) paying each partner rateably what is due to him on account of capital;
- (d) the residue, if any, is divided among partners in their profit-sharing ratio.
- In the books this is reflected through the Realisation Account, then the partners' loan accounts, then the capital accounts, which finally close against cash or bank.
